WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.580
Researcher Westrin selected 150 glass cups
filled with strawberry jelly for experimentation.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.920
The first 50 cups were placed into the Clockworks
on the setting "Rough."

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.630
The output produced was a pile of glass shards
and strawberry jelly.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.700
The second 50 cups were placed on the setting
"1:1."

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.960
The output produced was 50 cups made from
hardened strawberry jelly, filled with molten

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:21.960
glass.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.090
The final 50 cups were placed on the setting
"Very fine."

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:29.950
The output was a glass item, resembling an
exact replica of a human skull, filled with

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.179
strawberry jelly.

00:00:31.179 --> 00:00:36.180
Note: When the glass skull was created, it
managed to move its "jaw" and vocalized the

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.680
word "squish" before becoming inert again.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:40.410
- Researcher Westrin

